{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/sec-fundamental-object-explication","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Prose","doco:Section"],"label":"sec:fundamental-object-explication","kind":"prose","title":"The fundamental object and the emergent gauge group","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-rigid-monoidal-vect"],"tags":["category-theory","tannaka-krein","pedagogy"],"text":"fundamental-object-explication.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"sec:fundamental-object-explication\"></a><p>We fix two pieces of notation, defined below: the <a href=\"#def:fundamental-object\">fundamental object</a> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V</code> — the self-dual simple object of categorical dimension <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code> that tensor-generates <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{C}</code> — and the <a href=\"#def:tannaka-dual\">Tannaka dual</a> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G = \\mathrm{Aut}^{\\otimes}(\\tau)</code>, the gauge group emergent from the fibre functor <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tau</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/fundamental-object-explication.md","heading":""}
